# Stow must not deploy these from the zsh package, which targets $HOME rather
# than a directory of its own.
#
# The pnpm artifacts come from running pnpm inside zsh/; .gitignore keeps them
# out of Git, but stow does not read .gitignore and would try to link them into
# $HOME, where they collide with the real ones. node_modules also holds only pnpm
# state files, so there is nothing in it worth deploying.
^/node_modules
^/package\.json$
^/pnpm-lock\.yaml$

# Documentation for this package. It belongs in the repository, but a copy in
# $HOME is just clutter.
^/CHEATSHEET\.md$
^/INSTALL\.md$
